        "content": "# Composition and Art Direction\n\n## Reference-delta loop\n\nWhen a user provides an image, first identify camera height and lens,\nforeground, main subject, horizon, terrain silhouette, vegetation density,\nlighting direction, atmospheric depth, palette, and water placement. Create or\nchoose a matching bookmark, build large forms first, capture the viewport, list\nthe meaningful visual differences, fix the top three, and capture again.\n\nDo not merely add similarly colored objects. Match composition, depth, scale,\nsilhouette, light, and the hierarchy of attention.\n\n## Hierarchy\n\nGive the player a foreground frame, a midground story subject, and a distant\norientation landmark. Make water, roads, ridgelines, and vegetation bands lead\nthe eye and clarify traversal. Preserve warm/cool separation and local contrast\naround the subject.\n\n## Specialized looks\n\n- Forest ravine: carved channel, layered canopy, understory, debris, wet\n  margins, moss, readable shafts, streambed detail, and a walkable route.\n- Alpine vista: massif silhouette, altitude/slope snow, valley canopy, clouds\n  among peaks, foreground frame, atmospheric depth, and long-distance fidelity.\n- Cinematic showcase: explicit bookmark, controlled lens/composition, filmic\n  lighting, color script, restrained motion, suitable high or ultra preset,\n  screenshot comparison, and optional flythrough.\n",
